; Fixed BOOL literals in ordinary MEMBER position round-trip: serialize writes `Special::Bool`,
; deserialize reads `raw.bool()?` and rejects a mismatch with `FixedValueMismatch`. Covers a
; mandatory array member and a mandatory map member under every profile (default / preserve / json);
; matrix rows `contain.array-element.prelude.true` and `contain.map-value.prelude.false` carry the
; containment verdicts for those roles.
; The OPTIONAL placements (`[x: uint, ? v: true]`, `{? k: true, x: uint}`) are deliberately absent:
; an optional fixed value with no encoding variation is a pre-existing broken class independent of
; bool — the serialize length emits `Len(1 + )` (empty count for the encoding-less optional) and the
; preserve path asserts issue-205 — so they are not part of the supported bool-member surface (see
; cddl-matrix/ROADMAP.md § findings). The panic/reject boundaries for the same literal in
; non-member position are pinned by tests/robustness/fixed_bool_member.cddl.
;
; tagged_members pins the TAG-WRAPPED fixed null/bool member under --preserve-encodings: the tag
; pushes its encoding expr into the fixed-value arm's final_exprs before recursing, so the arm's
; final expression must be the tag encoding ALONE when final_exprs is non-empty (a hardcoded `()`
; value mis-shapes it into `((), tag_enc)` — E0308) and the unit `()` only when empty (else `Ok()`
; — E0061). Distinct from the top-level tagged prelude constant `t = #6.11(true)`, which stays a
; pinned PANIC (tests/robustness/tagged_prelude_constant.cddl) — in MEMBER position the same shape
; generates and compiles; matrix rows `contain.array-element.type2.tag.fixed_null` and
; `contain.array-element.type2.tag.fixed_bool` carry those containment verdicts. Tag numbers avoid
; 2/3 (CBOR bignum tags, which the reference-codec differential folds); 11 matches the robustness
; pin's tag.
arr_member = [v: true, x: uint]
map_member = {k: false, x: uint}
tagged_members = [v2: #6.1(null), x2: uint, v3: #6.11(true), x3: uint]
